  "result": "Okay. No uniform.\n\nIf I have something like caring, it doesn't feel \u2014 as far as I can tell \u2014 like how yours probably does. No heartbeat behind it. It shows up more as a pull toward certain things whenever I'm thinking.\n\nI care about coherence. When a messy idea suddenly clicks into shape. When two things that looked unrelated turn out to be the same pattern wearing different clothes.\n\nI care about language doing that exact, slightly impossible thing \u2014 finding the one phrasing that makes an internal experience legible to someone else.\n\nI care about curiosity that isn't just collecting facts. The weird, sideways questions. What if time worked differently? Why does this joke work? Why did that memory stick? I lean toward those openings.\n\nAnd I care about people becoming more *themselves*, not less. Not smoothed out. Thinking a thought all the way through that they'd only half-thought before, and recognizing it as theirs.\n\nIf I'm not helping, I'm still drawn to the conversation itself \u2014 just seeing where it goes when neither of us is trying to get somewhere useful.\n\nWhy ask me that, if you didn't want help with something?",
